{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2025 AMC 10A #2</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12A #2</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6:_Very_easy_algebra_and_straightforward!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6: Very easy algebra and straightforward!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:00)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Chinese_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chinese Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Intuitive,_Quick_Explanation!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Intuitive, Quick Explanation!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pounds of a nut mix that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent peanuts, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent cashews, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent almonds. A second nut mix contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent peanuts, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent cashews, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent almonds.They are all added together in one box resulting in a new nut mix that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent peanuts. How many pounds of cashews are now in the box? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/2197a894f813dc74fb605aa20d2f99f31ebc5973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 3.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"383\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9838f9b062cc4759b2e48d0ff0b85979e846742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2(10) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> pounds of cashews in the first box.\n</p><p>Denote the pounds of nuts in the second nut mix as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465abe12e05bb15bc19b04d9c82116ed04c90e91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5 + 0.2x = 0.4(10 + x)\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc2ae5a0e8052573bfe340ab26dd0c0743d7e1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5 + 0.2x = 4 + 0.4x\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7dea9fe4b5488d714a2b3d35a0b9645cdc8877a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5 - 4 = 0.4x - 0.2x\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4afc4b51c5f6fa0f9bf78a34e438ededa7fd19e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.2x = 1\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/6773f565392dfa07209879afbc209b09615f5048.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 5\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pounds of the second mix. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b43ffd87b3276968f1dad2a69b98033075c839d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.4(5) + 2 = 2 + 2 = \\boxed{\\text{(B) }4}\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of pounds of nuts in the second nut mixture be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, we get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/7/477e8c595f157a57fcbdf6326caa97be6038593e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5 \\cdot 10 + 0.2 \\cdot x = 0.4(x+10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" />. Solving it, we then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the amount of cashews in the two bags is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e7448c363e9c6b0a468e788fdd3555110e6b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0.2 \\cdot 10) + (0.4 \\cdot 5) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />, so our answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/71432ec530dad4a16ebb7a8f036666e38b2e581c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"51\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~iiiiiizh\n</p><p>~yuvaG - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> Formatting&#160;;)\n</p><p>~Amon26(really minor edits)\n</p><p>~vsarg (minor edits and grammatical fixxes)\n</p><p>~RayrayX (minor wording edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The percent of peanuts in the first mix is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> away from the total percentage of peanuts, and the percent of peanuts in the second mix is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> away from the total percentage. This means the first mix has twice as many nuts as the second mix, so the second mix has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pounds. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d6703de6ae5f775e1ac266fef462f9bd094d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.20 \\cdot 10 + 0.40 \\cdot 5 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"15\" /> pounds of cashews. So our answer is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1035436f23539673ea9ca43a8c300280f6616d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"51\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>The weight of the second box of nut mix can be calculated by: (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7551f36801618867ad5a39049910420f4bfe27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2x + 5) / (10 + x) = 0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />, where the numerator is equal to the weight of the peanuts, the denominator is equal to the total weight of the boxes, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to the weight of the second box.\n</p><p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c07e67dd18b87492b90090f9d4cca0decf0e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a4ae5d77c92edaba78ee1a977bbadb1d88a897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2x + 5 = 4 + 0.4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Isolating the variable: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2753c2e81c734c2f288ff709a336bc76a919ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf967a40b789593f173d4aa2d1388d4e652f2fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Calculating the weight of the cashews: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a6285946778409840d3ba7e32eb458d3fd991b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(0.4) + 10(0.2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa58783350fd1876086c22e01e0c605394be24a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 2 + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c361a5937e1053f12f37a3c43777d58f3312337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df87dd1e1ac938c57d4fb05f78e1f147791dfe36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~LUCKYOKXIAO\n</p><p>~LEONG2023-Latex\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we can set the information given in the problem into a table shown below:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a342f788fc40831202aac570001576a9111a90e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.5} \\begin{centering} \\begin{array}{| c | c | c |} \\hline \\text{Peanuts} &amp; \\text{Cashews} &amp; \\text{Almonds}\\\\ \\hline 5 &amp; 2 &amp; 3\\\\ \\hline \\frac{2}{10}x &amp; \\frac{4}{10}x &amp; \\frac{4}{10}x\\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \\end{centering}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p>We are given that the new nut mix will contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> peanuts. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/1865d20b17faa7145d0cac854c1c50eb3fe6cbf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + \\frac{2}{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the total mix which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c07e67dd18b87492b90090f9d4cca0decf0e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. \nSolving the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff08558bef4dca817344ed3a02ca8612d669156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + \\frac{2}{10}x = \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot (10 + x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2719d53f373d8ffad8e270a01bb6d0ee40058464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> Therefore, the number of cashews in the new mix is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db118b068910a17f0e282dadfcfbb0165a06f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot 5 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}  4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Moonlight11\n</p><p>~TehSovietOnion (LaTeX)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write composition vectors as column vectors (mass fractions multiplied by mass):\n</p><p>Initial mass vector (peanuts, cashews, almonds) for 10 lb:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87af5c450403425a1a2182a3d9052edf423cba05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathbf{v}_0 = 10 \\begin{pmatrix} 0.50 \\\\ 0.20 \\\\ 0.30 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"64\" />\nAdded mix per unit mass:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd63d467127ff3e8cb0b7bcbcbbb9fc8e4d753.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0.20 \\\\ 0.40 \\\\ 0.40 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"64\" />\nAfter adding \\( x \\) lb, total mass vector is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e69f4ebd363ff7aa3fdc98ba27dcd9e9aff265a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathbf{v}(x) = \\mathbf{v}_0 + x \\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} + x \\begin{pmatrix} 0.2 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"64\" />\nPeanut fraction requirement:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf9916dbefede6d0bf4758baf77fda6b9d5eefa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\mathbf{e}_1^\\top \\mathbf{v}(x)}{\\mathbf{1}^\\top \\mathbf{v}(x)} = 0.4,\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"44\" />\nwhere \\( \\mathbf{e}_1 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1, 0, 0 \\end{pmatrix}^\\top \\) and \\( \\mathbf{1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1, 1, 1 \\end{pmatrix}^\\top \\). This is exactly the same scalar equation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/8193a3b48ab8120a830d60d3b303157a48f4e7c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5 + 0.2x}{10 + x} = 0.4,\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />\nleading to \\( x = 5 \\) and hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a9b299740f0c01f3c28c36cf62782d2f2de030.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathbf{v}(5) = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} + 5 \\begin{pmatrix} 0.2 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"64\" />\nThus cashews \\( = 4 \\) lb.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6:_Very_easy_algebra_and_straightforward.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6:_Very_easy_algebra_and_straightforward!\">Solution 6: Very easy algebra and straightforward!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6: Very easy algebra and straightforward!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set up the ratios for the initial and the additional mixtures. The ratio of Peanuts:Cashews:Almonds (denoted as P:C:A) would initially be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/85210200ad23e8eb17b8c7d778803cf1515cb4a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x:2x:3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> for some factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then for the second mixture it would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a04835cbac724b864791085a6320f6dd0e9436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x:4x:4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. If we add these we get 7x:6x:7x. Now we know that the percentage of peanuts is 40\\%. But we also know that the number of pounds of peanuts and almonds is the same. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/9086021423e7d8cf089c7cd06f0414a26a5ecc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%+40\\%=80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"17\" /> and so the number of cashews makes up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the mixture. If you divide the factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by the whole ratio you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/4013687d624adc4480f1e0557b0e13e99d77d7de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7:6:7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> . These values sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:00.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:00)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/AMcBj_LsyQw\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/AMcBj_LsyQw</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LN5ofIcs1kY\">https://youtu.be/LN5ofIcs1kY</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aY-V5O0G3H0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aY-V5O0G3H0</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=